<title>POLAND: Zloty fixed touch softer at 2.93 pct from parity.</title>
<headline>Zloty fixed touch softer at 2.93 pct from parity.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-02-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>The National Bank of Poland fixed the zloty at 3.0400 to the dollar, up from 3.0470 on Friday and at 1.8145 to the mark, down from 1.8090, the NBP said.</p>
<p>The central bank fixed the zloty at an average of 2.93 percent from the weighted dollar and mark parity rates, a fraction weaker than Thursday's 2.96 percent fix.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
</text>
